{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>A sabbath of solemn rest it is.</b> A legal rule is written with yod, and that of parashat Emor with vav, and both are read as they are written, with samekh-yod; and ends ותאכל היא והוא." "<b>For you.</b> This is Yom HaKippurim, which is sanctified on your account; but the seventh day is called a sabbat לה'."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "The comment appears to reference spelling or pointing variants between the phrase as written here and in parashat Emor (Lev 23:32); the reference to ותאכל היא והוא (Deut 5:14) seems to introduce a cross-reference to the Sabbath command, though its syntactic connection is unclear.", 1 "The comment is abbreviated; לה' presumably expands to ליהוה, 'to YHWH' (cf. Lev 23:3)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:13:01.188985664Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}